course: dictionary
lesson: 5524
title: Leatherback: a word from the ocean
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A leatherback is a kind of sea turtle. The word has a clue in it: leather is tough skin, and its shell is covered with tough, leathery skin instead of hard plates. «Leatherback turtles eat huge amounts of jellyfish» tells you what it eats.
explain: Context helps you work out which animal is meant. Look at what the sentences have in common: sea, jellyfish, and floating plastic bags. Every one is about ocean life, so leatherback is an animal, not a place or a thing you can wear.
explain: Try your meaning in the sentences. «A floating plastic bag looks like a jellyfish to a leatherback» still makes sense if a leatherback is a large sea turtle. If your meaning fits every sentence, you are probably right. If not, check a dictionary.
fact: A leatherback is the largest turtle in the world.
fact: Its shell is covered with tough, leathery skin instead of hard plates.
fact: Leatherbacks eat jellyfish, and their throats are lined with spikes that stop the slippery food sliding back out.
fact: «Plastic bags» can look like jellyfish to a leatherback, so plastic in the sea can be very dangerous for them.
fact: Leatherback is a noun: one leatherback, two leatherbacks. Phrases: leatherback turtle, leatherback sea turtle.
exercise: What is a leatherback? | *A sea turtle, the largest turtle in the world | A type of jellyfish | A plastic bag that floats on the sea | A sea bird with long wings
exercise: «Sea turtles sometimes eat plastic bags, mistaking them for jellyfish.» Why do they make this mistake? | Jellyfish are made of plastic | They like the taste of plastic | They are trying to build a nest | *A floating plastic bag can look like a jellyfish
exercise: «Leatherback turtles eat huge amounts of jellyfish.» Find and copy one word that tells you they eat a lot. | amounts | turtles | jellyfish | *huge
test: What does «leathery» mean in «tough, leathery skin»? | Shiny like glass | Hard like a rock | Soft and wet like a sponge | *Tough and like leather
test: «Archelon was a sea turtle about 75 million years ago, longer than a car, like today's leatherback.» What does like mean here? | *Similar to | Except for | Near | Enjoying
exam: Read «A floating plastic bag looks like a jellyfish to a leatherback, which is one big reason to keep plastic out of the sea.» Why is plastic in the sea a danger? | *Leatherbacks may mistake it for food and swallow it | Leatherbacks use plastic to build their nests | Plastic bags are too heavy to float | Plastic makes the sea too salty for jellyfish
